WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.920
More than 400 gigawatts of plan datacenter load is now chasing power. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres,

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:13.100
Episode 36. After that, a nan stacking plan, an intel quantum buy, a packaging price report,

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:18.660
and the advanced payments that buy a place in line. Industrial info resources expects

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.800
Microsoft, Meta, Amazon, and Google to announce more than $700 billion of datacenter spending

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.360
this year. Data center knowledge carried those remarks from Data Center World Power in September.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:37.960
The same four companies announced to combine $64 billion in 2018. The United States now has 53

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:45.600
gigawatts of operational data center load up from 23 gigawatts in 2023. Another 42 gigawatts is

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:54.380
approved or under construction. IIR frames demand as moving from 35 gigawatts in 2024 to 125 gigawatts

00:00:54.380 --> 00:01:01.320
by 2030. Almost 100 US sites are drawn for at least one gigawatt each. The US and Canada

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:09.980
pipeline in that count is about $4.75 trillion, across more than 4,250 projects. IIR has

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:17.020
more than 500 data center moratorium on record in 42 states. $130 billion of projects were

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:22.600
rejected in the first quarter of 2026 alone. New York has a temporary ban on new data

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:28.040
centers larger than 50 megawatts. Texas has paused new grid interconnections while it works

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:34.560
through about 200 gigawatts of requests. GE, Vernova, Mitsubishi Power, and Siemens Energy are

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:42.080
sold out of larger gas turbines through 2029. Some of those orders run into 2031. Shane Mullins of

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:49.700
IIR said that above 300 megawatts, if the utility queue says 2034, building or contracting a gas plant

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.440
is the fastest path to power.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.960
IAR counts 228 billion dollars of gas plant projects,

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.640
347 of them, counting new builds, expansions, and conversions.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.440
Nuclear is 111 projects worth $311.4 billion,

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.860
including 61 small modular reactors.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.440
Battery storage is 701 projects worth almost $200 billion.

00:02:14.738 --> 00:02:17.298
Micron has announced a plan, not a shipment,

00:02:17.738 --> 00:02:19.178
for 400-layer NAND.

00:02:19.938 --> 00:02:27.998
TechPowerUp reports the G11 parts are aimed at the second half of 2027, using wafer to wafer stacking to double module capacity.

00:02:28.738 --> 00:02:32.278
G9, which is shipping now, uses more than 200 layers.

00:02:32.898 --> 00:02:42.138
One wafer holds the memory cells and the other holds the peripheral logic, joined by hybrid bonding, the structural idea YMTC already uses an X stacking.

00:02:42.918 --> 00:02:44.538
Intel has agreed to buy classic.

00:02:44.538 --> 00:02:49.312
tech power-up, citing the company announcement, calls it a definitive agreement.

00:02:49.932 --> 00:02:54.692
After Intel said the same on X, the combination is Intel's quantum software,

00:02:55.252 --> 00:02:59.892
its silicon-spin-cubit work, and its manufacturing, plus classics automated

00:02:59.892 --> 00:03:04.572
algorithm synthesis platform. That software is meant to stay agnostic to

00:03:04.572 --> 00:03:08.972
qubit type and to the hardware underneath. Lipbootan said the deal turns

00:03:08.972 --> 00:03:13.312
Intel's quantum computing group into a full-stack quantum computing business.

00:03:13.312 --> 00:03:20.762
Analyst Jeff Poo says Elon Musk wanted 30,000 of NVIDIA's latest AI GPU systems and is

00:03:20.762 --> 00:03:21.822
getting 20,000.

00:03:22.342 --> 00:03:26.922
WCC FETTECH reports that Poo still calls that enough to make him the biggest buyer

00:03:26.922 --> 00:03:28.042
in 2027.

00:03:28.742 --> 00:03:31.642
That is an analyst claim, not an NVIDIA shipment notice.

00:03:32.739 --> 00:03:38.419
Business reports developers have secured 10 TSMC suppliers for the $7 billion Halo Vista

00:03:38.419 --> 00:03:39.419
mixed use project.

00:03:39.899 --> 00:03:43.119
That is a supplier commitment, not a reported energization.

00:03:43.119 --> 00:03:48.859
A reported co-woast price increase is the new piece on packaging, which yesterday was still

00:03:48.859 --> 00:03:50.059
a capacity question.

00:03:50.559 --> 00:03:57.179
China Time Sources, carried by WCC FETTECH and Yahoo Finance, say TSMC is discussing a rise

00:03:57.179 --> 00:03:58.679
of 10-20%.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.899
TSMC has not confirmed it.

00:04:01.259 --> 00:04:07.339
The reported load is AI-GPUs, custom ASICs, and server CPUs, with more compute dies and

00:04:07.339 --> 00:04:09.319
more HBM stacks on one package.

00:04:09.319 --> 00:04:15.139
Bigger packages cut how many units a tool finishes in an hour, and the test time gets longer.

00:04:16.179 --> 00:04:24.179
WCCFETTEK puts the reported bill at 130,000 monthly waifers in 2026 and 200,000 units in 2027.

00:04:24.899 --> 00:04:34.519
Yahoo, citing the same China Times report, says monthly capacity should exceed 130,000 units in 2026 and 200,000 units the next year.

00:04:34.519 --> 00:04:37.659
Those two accounts do not use the same unit word.

00:04:38.159 --> 00:04:42.919
Sources in the WCCFET tech piece say a new advanced packaging plant takes about three

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:45.479
years to hit full load at the bottleneck stations.

00:04:46.159 --> 00:04:50.219
Equipment lead times have stretched from three to six months to six to eight months.

00:04:51.139 --> 00:04:55.119
TSMC's five times radical co-woast packages are in volume production.

00:04:55.799 --> 00:05:01.499
Nine times and 14 times versions are in development, and panel-based co-poss is aimed at larger

00:05:01.499 --> 00:05:03.039
packages and a lower cost.

00:05:03.039 --> 00:05:10.179
Yahoo names Nvidia, AMD, Broadcom, Qualcomm, and MediaTek among the customers who would pay a higher

00:05:10.179 --> 00:05:16.696
packaging price. Anthropic told the US Securities and Exchange Commission in a registration statement

00:05:16.696 --> 00:05:22.716
filed October 26th that most of the world's most advanced chip making sits at TSMC in Taiwan.

00:05:23.336 --> 00:05:29.356
Businessline reported the filing. Anthropic said a military conflict, tariffs and trade restrictions,

00:05:29.356 --> 00:05:34.756
conditions, economic coercion, a blockade, a natural disaster, or a loss of electricity

00:05:34.756 --> 00:05:37.796
or water could severely disrupt advanced chip supply.

00:05:38.376 --> 00:05:43.336
Capacity outside Taiwan, including in the United States, is still early stage, the filing

00:05:43.336 --> 00:05:43.676
says.

00:05:44.296 --> 00:05:49.856
It also says TSMC has at times been unable to meet full demand, leaving anthropic short

00:05:49.856 --> 00:05:50.836
of chips on time.

00:05:51.536 --> 00:05:57.536
Soul Economic Daily, reading the same filing, says anthropic names SK Heinex, Samsung Electronics

00:05:57.536 --> 00:06:00.596
and micron as the main high-band with memory producers.

00:06:01.236 --> 00:06:06.276
The company warns those three may not deliver the volumes on time, especially if other

00:06:06.276 --> 00:06:08.456
large buyers lock a supplier's output.

00:06:09.136 --> 00:06:14.096
That paper's simple sum of seven disclose contracts is about $637 billion.

00:06:14.996 --> 00:06:20.736
The largest piece is a Broadcom AI Accelerator lease of about $161.2 billion.

00:06:20.736 --> 00:06:28.236
dollars. Google is at least 114.5 billion, Amazon at least 110 billion, and Microsoft

00:06:28.236 --> 00:06:35.836
at least 44.9 billion. SpaceX AI, NScale and Lambda are in the set as well. The paper says

00:06:35.836 --> 00:06:40.436
that total mixes minimum spending, equipment leases, and amounts that move with volume,

00:06:40.856 --> 00:06:45.756
so it is not one fixed investment. Anthropics computing and infrastructure costs were

00:06:45.756 --> 00:06:51.636
$8.945 billion in the first half of this year, up 283%.

00:06:52.056 --> 00:06:57.936
Revenue in that half rose to $16.286 billion, from $1.163 billion.

00:06:58.958 --> 00:07:04.018
A finished accelerator still has to meet memory, a substrate, and a test socket, and any

00:07:04.018 --> 00:07:05.338
one of those can hold the shipment.

00:07:06.518 --> 00:07:09.338
36KR describes the old chain as a clean split.

00:07:09.938 --> 00:07:15.058
Design houses specified the part, foundries built the wafer, and packaging and tests took

00:07:15.058 --> 00:07:20.378
the next step, joined by orders and shared standards. That split assumed each link could

00:07:20.378 --> 00:07:25.658
be booked after the one before it. AI parts broke the sequence because the process, the

00:07:25.658 --> 00:07:31.038
memory and the package set the ceiling together. A larger die also eats more wafer and more

00:07:31.038 --> 00:07:37.738
package area per chip, so a miss in one input idols the others. Trend Force in a March 2026

00:07:37.738 --> 00:07:46.578
estimate that 36 kr sites put full-year foundry revenue up 24.8% to about 218.8 billion dollars.

00:07:47.178 --> 00:07:53.278
The same estimate said TSMC's 5 nanometer, 4 nanometer, and more advanced lines would stay fully

00:07:53.278 --> 00:08:01.678
loaded through the end of 2026. 36 kr says that load is Nvidia and AMD GPUs, plus custom chips from

00:08:01.678 --> 00:08:07.378
Google, AWS, and Meta. A full advanced node line does not finish the chip if the package,

00:08:07.918 --> 00:08:14.398
the substrate, or the test insertion is late. In July, 2026, AMCore signed a $1.5 billion

00:08:14.398 --> 00:08:19.818
multi-year advance packaging agreement with NVIDIA, and the advance payment was to fund

00:08:19.818 --> 00:08:27.258
US capacity. On October 21st, the two added a South Korea expansion. 36KR puts the US and

00:08:27.258 --> 00:08:29.298
Korea agreements together at $3 billion.

00:08:30.158 --> 00:08:36.378
Nvidia also put $1.1 billion down with King Euan Electronics to fund a U.S. test factory

00:08:36.378 --> 00:08:37.598
and the tools to run it.

00:08:38.118 --> 00:08:44.058
Substrate deals that same day, with Ibedin, Samsung Electromechanics, and Xinxing Electronics,

00:08:44.338 --> 00:08:48.798
are planned to take relevant substrate capacity to 2.5 times the current level.

00:08:49.518 --> 00:08:54.378
Ibedin's expansion of its Ono plant in Japan is backed by an Nvidia advance as well.

00:08:54.378 --> 00:08:58.998
cash in a multi-year volume promise move a build plan earlier than a spot

00:08:58.998 --> 00:09:04.598
order would. 36K are notes that 2.5D packaging of the co-woast type has been

00:09:04.598 --> 00:09:09.098
tight since 2023 and that the squeeze has spread to packaging equipment,

00:09:09.598 --> 00:09:14.438
substrates and key materials. More wafers or a larger packaging house still

00:09:14.438 --> 00:09:18.758
leave delivery gated by whichever input did not get the check. The same

00:09:18.758 --> 00:09:22.478
piece warns that firms with capital and long order commitments take the

00:09:22.478 --> 00:09:27.598
scarce capacity first. A reservation clears the bottleneck only for those buyers when

00:09:27.598 --> 00:09:32.698
the missing part is a tool. A substrate or a material the prepaid supplier cannot pull

00:09:32.698 --> 00:09:36.278
forward. And it leaves out the buyer who cannot fund the factory.

00:09:36.878 --> 00:09:42.678
On the horizon, King Ewan's US test factory has a mass production target of April 2027.

00:09:43.318 --> 00:09:49.798
The substrate plan announced October 21, 2026 runs across the next three years. Also

00:09:49.798 --> 00:09:54.658
Also today, shipping manifests and an internal driver reported by Tom's hardware and tech

00:09:54.658 --> 00:10:02.218
power-up show unannounced LGA 1700 parts called Raptor Lake Next, including a 16-core 125

00:10:02.218 --> 00:10:10.118
watt chip at 3.5 gigahertz with 30 megabytes of cash and a 20-core 65 watt chip at 2.1

00:10:10.118 --> 00:10:12.118
gigahertz with 33 megabytes.

00:10:12.698 --> 00:10:18.298
Northern Arizona University and TSMC are offering career training that does not require a degree.

